-- title:
--   Jointly injective local points on a Hecke–Galois datum
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers. Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S)`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Let $T$ be a noetherian local ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, an $\mathcal O$-algebra whose structure map is local and which is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module. Assume every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$, and assume given a datum `HeckeGaloisRepDatum N (↑S) 𝒪 θ T`: a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ reducing to $\theta$ modulo the maximal ideals, with $\mathcal O[\pi(\mathbb T)] = T$, with the property that every ring homomorphism $\chi$ from the Hecke algebra to $\mathcal O$ reducing to $\theta$ factors as $\psi \circ \pi$ for some $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi \colon T \to \mathcal O$, with $\mathcal O \to T \to T/\mathfrak m_T$ surjective, together with a rank-two adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ are $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. The conclusion asserts the existence of an $n$ and of rings $A_0, \dots, A_{n-1}$, each a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and a module-finite $\mathcal O$-algebra with local structure map, together with $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphisms $\chi_i \colon T \to A_i$, each a local homomorphism, which are jointly injective: if $\chi_i(x) = 0$ for all $i$ then $x = 0$.
--
--   This expresses that the coefficient ring of a weight-two Hecke–Galois datum, for $S$ containing the primes dividing $N$, is reduced and embeds into a finite product of complete discrete valuation rings by local $\mathcal O$-algebra maps, so that identities in $T$ may be checked after specialisation at the individual characteristic-zero points. It is used in the analysis of the local behaviour of $\rho$ at primes exactly dividing the level, in [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isUnipotentOnInertiaAt_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isUnipotentOnInertiaAt_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd).
